WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
In Sri Lanka, a family sits
beside a dying grandmother,

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.230
reminding her of the good she has done.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.150
After she dies, relatives pour
water into a cup until it overflows,

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.020
while monks chant.

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.800
The monks chant a verse about how
all things arise and pass away.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.190
Yet Buddhists teach that nothing
fixed, no unchanging soul,

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.870
moves on at death.

8
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.870
So why hold rites for the dead at all?

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.160
In this mission, you'll see how Buddhist
teaching on death shapes what families

10
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.140
do when someone dies.

11
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.860
Then you'll weigh up whether these
rites are really for the living,

12
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.730
or for the dead.

13
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: find out why Buddhists
hold rites for the dead when they believe

14
00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.110
there is no fixed soul.
